{
  "title": "Question words, connectors and frequency",
  "note": "Question words sit where the answer would go, and the sentence ends in か: トイレはどこですか. A question word cannot take は; use が: だれが来ますか. あまり (not very) and 全然 (not at all) need a negative verb: あまり食べません. から after a clause gives a reason: 寒いですから.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Tae Kim's Guide to Learning Japanese",
    "u": "https://guidetojapanese.org/learn/grammar"
  },
  "items": [
